    settings_gamemode: 'Game mode', settings_gamemode_hint: 'Pauses animated effects while gaming', settings_gamemode_need_tool: 'Optional: install PresentMon to show real in-game FPS in the system panel. Game detection already works without it.', settings_gamemode_install: 'Install PresentMon', settings_gamemode_installing: 'Installing PresentMon…', settings_gamemode_installed: 'PresentMon installed', settings_gamemode_install_failed: 'Installation failed', settings_gamemode_mangohud_missing: 'In-game FPS needs MangoHud: install it from your distribution\'s package manager (for example “sudo dnf install mangohud” or “sudo apt install mangohud”), then launch the game through it — on Steam, set “mangohud %command%” as a launch option. Game detection already works without it.', settings_gamemode_mangohud_ready: 'MangoHud is installed. FPS only appear for games launched through it: on Steam set “mangohud %command%” as a launch option, elsewhere run the game as “mangohud ./game”. On Linux there is no way to read a game\'s frame rate without the game\'s cooperation.', settings_senshist_title: 'Sensor history', settings_senshist_hint: 'Records temperatures and load over time for the history charts', settings_senshist_enable: 'Enable', settings_senshist_enable_hint: 'One sample every 5 minutes from data already read; everything stays on your PC. No AI required.', settings_gpu_title: 'Rendering GPU', settings_gpu_hint: 'Which graphics card the browser draws the dashboard on', settings_gpu_current: 'Current GPU', settings_gpu_tip: 'The browser is rendering on a discrete GPU (above). If your Xeneon Edge is driven by a different, integrated GPU, every frame is copied between the two cards — keeping the discrete GPU awake even when the dashboard is idle. To pin the browser to the integrated GPU: Windows Settings → System → Display → Graphics, add your browser and set it to “Power saving”.',
